---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Wordmark from "../../components/Wordmark.astro";
import LangSwitch from "../../components/LangSwitch.astro";
const home = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "")}/en/`;
const contact = "mail@ardeman.com";
const alternates = { id: "privasi/", en: "en/privacy/" };
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Krida"
  description="What data Krida uses, what for, and who receives it."
  lang="en"
  alternates={alternates}
>
  <main>
    <header class="nav">
      <a class="logo" href={home}><Wordmark height={30} /></a>
      <LangSwitch lang="en" alternates={alternates} />
    </header>

    <article class="doc">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="doc-date">Effective 12 November 2026</p>

      <p>
        Krida is a collection of board games for Android and iPhone, made by Ardeman. This page explains what data
        the Krida app uses, what for, and who receives it.
      </p>

      <h2>In short</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Krida can be played without an account, and does not ask for your email, phone number, or contacts.</li>
        <li>An account is optional (Sign in with Apple or Google). We keep the account ID Apple or Google gives us,
          your display name and avatar choice (and for Google, the picture URL when you use that photo), and you can
          delete the account from the app at any time.</li>
        <li>Online play goes through a relay that only forwards game traffic while a room is open; it does not keep
          a history of games.</li>
        <li>Ads in Krida are provided by Google AdMob, which collects some device data as described below.</li>
        <li>Payments are processed by Google Play or the App Store; we never see your payment details.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Data stored on your device</h2>
      <p>
        Settings (such as sound and music), the status of the <i>Remove ads</i> purchase, and — if you leave a
        running online or nearby game — a short rejoin token for that room are stored on your own device and are
        not sent to us as a profile. This data is deleted when you uninstall the app, or when you forget the room
        from the menu.
      </p>

      <h2>Playing together nearby (Bluetooth and Wi-Fi)</h2>
      <p>
        When you play with friends nearby, Krida uses Bluetooth or the same Wi-Fi network to send game data (the
        room code, player names in the room, and game moves) directly between devices. That data does not pass
        through our servers and is not kept after the game ends.
      </p>
      <p>
        On Android 11 and earlier, Android requires the location permission to search for nearby Bluetooth devices.
        Krida asks for that permission only to find people to play with; Krida does not read, store, or send your
        location.
      </p>

      <h2>Playing together online</h2>
      <p>
        When you play online (a room by code or link, a public lobby, or quick match), your phone connects to our
        relay at <code>krida-relay.ardeman.com</code>, run on Cloudflare Workers. The relay only forwards bytes
        between the host phone and the guests; it does not understand or change the game.
      </p>
      <p>
        While you are connected, the relay necessarily sees your IP address and the game traffic it forwards (room
        codes, seat names chosen in the lobby, moves, and the same lobby status needed to keep the room running).
        That traffic is not kept as a log or a history of games. The relay holds only the short-lived state needed
        for an open room (for example the host's reconnect key, whether the lobby is public, and seat reservations)
        and deletes the room when it ends or after a short idle period. We do not sell this data or use it for
        advertising.
      </p>
      <p>
        Cloudflare processes the connection as part of running the Workers platform under
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's Privacy Policy</a>. Krida does not use
        Cloudflare Analytics or other Cloudflare products that would build a player profile from this traffic.
      </p>

      <h2>Ads (Google AdMob)</h2>
      <p>
        Krida shows ads from Google AdMob. To show ads, measure their performance, and prevent fraud, Google may
        collect:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>the device's advertising ID (Advertising ID on Android);</li>
        <li>IP address and the approximate location derived from it;</li>
        <li>device and app information, such as model, system version, and language;</li>
        <li>interactions with ads, such as impressions and clicks;</li>
        <li>diagnostic data, such as load times and errors.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        In regions that require it (such as the European Union and the United Kingdom), Krida shows Google's consent
        form before any ad loads, and you can change your choice at any time from the app. On iPhone, Krida does not
        request tracking permission (App Tracking Transparency), so the iPhone advertising ID (IDFA) is not used.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can reset your advertising ID or turn off personalized ads in your device settings. Google explains how
        it uses this data in
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites?hl=en">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>
        and the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy?hl=en">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>Once you buy <i>Remove ads</i>, Krida stops loading ads.</p>

      <h2>In-app purchases</h2>
      <p>
        The <i>Remove ads</i> purchase is processed entirely by Google Play or the Apple App Store under their own
        privacy policies. Krida only receives confirmation that the purchase succeeded; we do not receive your name,
        email, or payment details.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Krida is intended for users aged 13 and over and does not knowingly collect personal data from children under
        13. If you are a parent and believe your child has given us data, contact us and we will help.
      </p>

      <h2 id="account">Account (optional)</h2>
      <p>
        You can sign in with Apple or Google from the account button in the menu. When you do, we store in the
        relay's database (Cloudflare D1): the account ID Apple or Google gives Krida, your display name, the
        avatar you choose (a shape and colours drawn in the app, or your Google profile picture), and when the
        account was created. For Google accounts we also keep the picture URL Google provides, so other players'
        phones can load that picture from Google when you pick it; we do not host the photo. We do not receive or
        store your email, password, or contacts. Your phone keeps a session token so you stay signed in.
      </p>
      <p>
        A signed-in account gets a friend code. When you or another player adds the other by code or friend link,
        we store that the two accounts are friends, and each of you sees the other's display name and avatar in
        the friends list. Either of you can remove the other at any time, which removes it for both.
      </p>
      <p>
        A friend hosting an online room can invite you. The invite (their name, the room and the game) is kept for
        two minutes. On an iPhone, if you allow notifications, we store the device's notification token with your
        session and send the invite through Apple's push service so it reaches you while the app is closed. The
        token is removed when you sign out or delete your account; you can turn notifications off in iOS Settings.
      </p>
      <p>
        To delete your account, open the account button in the menu and choose "Delete account". The account, name,
        avatar, Google picture URL, friend code, friends list, notification tokens and every session are removed
        from our database right away; for Apple accounts, Krida's access at Apple is revoked too. If you can't open
        the app, email the address under Contact and we will delete the account.
      </p>

      <h2>Deleting data</h2>
      <p>
        Without an account, uninstalling the app deletes all Krida data on your device; an account is deleted from
        the app as described above. Data Google
        collects for ads is managed by Google; you can manage it in your device's ad settings or your Google account.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes, the latest version will be posted on this page with a new effective date.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about privacy? Email <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>.</p>
    </article>

    <footer class="footer">
      <a href={home}>Back to Krida</a>
      <span class="footer-copy"
        >krida.ardeman.com · <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "")}/en/changelog/`}>Changelog</a></span
      >
    </footer>
  </main>
</Base>
